    {
      "v": 7,
      "zh": "我要赐他们认识我的心，知道我是耶和华。他们要作我的子民，我要作他们的　神，因为他们要一心归向我。」",
      "en": "I will give them the desire to acknowledge that I[NOTE:1] am the Lord. I will be their God, and they will be my people. For they will wholeheartedly[NOTE:2] return to me.’",
      "notes": [
        "Heb “I will give them a heart to know me, that I am the Lord.” For the use of “heart” here referring to “inclinations, resolutions, and determinations of the will,” see BDB 525 s.v. לֵב 4 and compare the usage in 2 Chr 12:14. For the use of “know” to mean “acknowledge,” see BDB 384 s.v. יָדַע Qal.1.f and compare the usage in Jer 39:4. For the construction “know ‘someone’ that he…” = “know that ‘someone’…,” see GKC 365 §117.h and compare the usage in 2 Sam 3:25.",
        "Heb “with all their heart.”"
